#: ../../guide/localization.md:1
msgid "Contributing Translations"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:3
msgid ""
"Translations live in the repository next to the code and are contributed by "
"pull request, the same as any other change. There is no translation platform "
"to sign up for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:5
msgid ""
"There are two independent sets of files: the VS Code extension, which uses "
"flat JSON, and the documentation, which uses gettext `.po` catalogs. Pick "
"whichever you want to work on — they do not depend on each other."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:7
msgid "How to contribute"
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:9
msgid "Fork the repository and branch off `main`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:10
msgid "Edit the files described below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:11
msgid "Run `just check-l10n` to verify the extension files are still in sync."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:12
msgid "Open a pull request."
msgstr ""

#: ../../guide/localization.md:14
msgid ""
"Partial work is fine. For the documentation, leave `msgstr \"\"` on anything "
"you have not translated and Sphinx falls back to English. For the extension, "
"every key must be present (see [CI Checks](#ci-checks)), so copy the English "
"string as the value for any key you skip."
msgstr ""

